    <item>
      <title>1. Population models</title>
      <link>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/fundamentals/population/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/fundamentals/population/</guid>
      <description>&lt;link rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; href=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/katex.min.css&#34; /&gt;&lt;script defer src=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/katex.min.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;script defer src=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/auto-render.min.js&#34; onload=&#34;renderMathInElement(document.body, {&amp;#34;delimiters&amp;#34;:[{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;$$&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;$$&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:true},{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\(&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\)&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:false},{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\[&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\]&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:true}]});&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-container-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;headline-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;Population models&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-text-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-text-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this chapter we discuss models for populations data. Those data&#xA;contain observations from a set of individuals sampled from a&#xA;population. Such data are characterized by one or more&#xA;observations for each individual. All the models&#xA;discussed here are &lt;em&gt;parameter models&lt;/em&gt;, in that observations are described&#xA;with models with parameters. These models are capable of explaining the&#xA;data variability due to the those unknown random parameters.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2. PK and ODEs</title>
      <link>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/fundamentals/pkode/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/fundamentals/pkode/</guid>
      <description>&lt;link rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; href=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/katex.min.css&#34; /&gt;&lt;script defer src=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/katex.min.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;script defer src=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/auto-render.min.js&#34; onload=&#34;renderMathInElement(document.body, {&amp;#34;delimiters&amp;#34;:[{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;$$&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;$$&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:true},{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\(&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\)&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:false},{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\[&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\]&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:true}]});&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-container-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;headline-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;Pharmacokinetics and ordinary differential equations&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-text-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-text-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Since pharmacokinetics (PK) always involves time \(t\), we make it explicit&#xA;in the population data formulation from the last chapter. To simplify&#xA;notation we also remove the subscripts for the moment:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;$$&#xA;y = f(x, \phi, t) + \epsilon.&#xA;$$&#xA;Here \(x\), \(y\), \(\phi\), and \(\epsilon\) can be vectors.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;For example, let us consider \(x=D\),&#xA;\(D\) being the single bolus dose amount, and \(\theta=(V, k)\) with \(V\)&#xA;for the volumne of distribution and \(k\) the elminination&#xA;coefficient, in one-compartment models.&#xA;For the plasma concentration observation \(y\), we have&#xA;$$&#xA;y=\frac{D}{V}e^{-kt} +\epsilon,&#xA;$$&#xA;thus the canonical form of \(f\) is&#xA;$$&#xA;F=f(D, (V, k), t)=\frac{D}{V}e^{-kt}&#xA;$$&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
